# Project Subterfuge Architecture

## What This Is
A social deduction party game (React Native + Expo + Firebase). Players receive secret targets and missions; eliminate your target without getting caught. Web-first, mobile-compatible.

## Tech Stack
- **Frontend:** React Native 0.81 / Expo 54 / Expo Router 6 (file-based routing)
- **Backend:** Firebase Firestore (real-time via `onSnapshot`), Firebase Anonymous Auth
- **Language:** TypeScript 5.9 (strict)
- **UI:** CSS-in-JS via `StyleSheet.create`, custom `theme.ts` tokens, "Cold War Bureau" aesthetic

## Folder Structure
```
client/
├── app/                          # Expo Router screens (file-based routes)
│   ├── _layout.tsx               # Root: fonts, auth, error boundary
│   ├── index.tsx                 # Welcome screen
│   └── game/
│       ├── [id].tsx              # Game room (tabs: Contract, Situation Room, Admin)
│       ├── configure.tsx         # Host: task pack & difficulty config
│       └── lobby.tsx             # Join / host / identity flow
├── src/
│   ├── components/               # Shared UI: Button, Input, Alert, AvatarSelector, ErrorBoundary
│   ├── constants.ts              # App-wide constants (durations, URLs, defaults)
│   ├── theme.ts                  # Design tokens (colors, spacing, typography)
│   ├── types/                    # TypeScript interfaces (Game, Player, TaskPack)
│   ├── data/                     # Static data: avatars, fallback tasks, seed CSV
│   ├── features/
│   │   ├── auth/AuthContext.tsx   # Anonymous auth provider
│   │   ├── game/
│   │   │   ├── gameService.ts    # Firestore CRUD (create, join, start, eliminate, etc.)
│   │   │   ├── gameLogic.ts      # Pure functions (shuffle, target chain, win detection)
│   │   │   ├── useGame.ts        # Real-time Firestore subscription hook
│   │   │   └── components/       # Game-specific UI (ContractView, CommandCenterView, etc.)
│   │   └── tasks/taskService.ts  # Firestore queries for packs/missions
│   ├── hooks/                    # useAlert, useHoldToConfirm
│   └── utils/                    # storage.ts, gameUtils.ts, avatarDisplay.ts
```

## Data Flow
1. Firestore is the **single source of truth** (no Redux, no Zustand)
2. `useGame(gameId)` subscribes via `onSnapshot` → returns `{ game, players, loading, error }`
3. Mutations go through `gameService.ts` → Firestore → `onSnapshot` pushes updates
4. Local React state is only for UI ephemera (loading flags, input values, modals)

## Key Patterns
- **Platform abstraction:** Never use `Alert.alert`, `SecureStore`, or `localStorage` directly. Use `useAlert()` and `storage.save/get/delete`.
- **Feature-based grouping:** Colocate service, hook, components, and types per feature.
- **Pure logic extraction:** `gameLogic.ts` contains testable pure functions; `gameService.ts` handles only Firestore I/O.
- **Constants:** Magic numbers go in `src/constants.ts`; colors go in `theme.ts`.

## Running
```bash
cd client && npm install && npx expo start --web   # localhost:8081
npm test                                            # Jest tests
npm run lint                                        # ESLint
```
